CPANSec (Robert) reported two CVEs on 2026-09-04. The standard window is 14
days, so publication falls on 2026-09-18; an extension or an earlier
publication can be requested.

CVE-2026-85783 -- unbounded stanza count. Fixed in k45.
CVE-2026-85782 -- secret key in exception messages. Already fixed in 0.003;
CPANSec may publish it as fixed.

TO DO
1. Send the reply. The text is written and lives at ~/cpansec-reply-crypt-age.md
   (reproduction with our own numbers, both halves of the fix, the finding that
   age and rage impose no limit at all, downstream status).
2. Upload, and pull the downstream pins afterwards (p5-file-sops k192,
   kubernetes-ocp k135).
3. ORDERING: CPANSec counts a public commit, PR or issue as publication. The
   fix commit describes the vulnerability in full, so pushing to
   github.com/Getty/p5-crypt-age publishes it. Doing that before the upload
   means the hole is public while the fix is not installable.

No key material in this ticket, no PoC data.

